    {
      "post_id": "85995",
      "author_handle": "aschilling",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 10 years 8 months ago",
      "body": "No way to know, but it is different every time, sometimes because of your past experience and expectation and sometimes because of the difference in how your second baby will feed.\nBut don't get upset or beat yourself up if it goes the same as the first time - just do your best and relax and it will be okay.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-9629/#85995",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/d5828195928cdeb7f823.html",
