      "role": "response",
      "original_post_id": "85204"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "86905",
      "author_handle": "tina122321",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 10 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "If you are worried it would be best to talk to a la leache league consultant or some other type of breast feeding expert before you even have the baby. They are usually free or very cheap and can help you have a plan in case this baby is hard to breast feed at first. They can even visit you right after the birth. My experiences with them have been very positive.\nI think you should talk to them, but I also think you should have confidence in yourself. You already breast fed a difficult to feed baby. You have experience and determination. You will get through this!",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-9629/#86905",
